 "notes": "POLARBEAR search for ALP-induced polarization angle oscillation of the Crab Nebula (Tau A), 150 GHz, 2015-2016. Headline result is the stochastic 95% upper bound (red curve / black smoothed curve in Fig. 11), primary science result. Points computed from the smoothed analytic approximation Eq. 47: g_agamma = 2.16e-12 GeV^-1 * (m_a/1e-21 eV) * [sinc(m_a/3.7e-19 eV)]^-1, with unnormalized sinc(x)=sin(x)/x (verified against Fig. 11: ~2e-12 at 1e-21 eV, rising steeply near 7.7e-19 eV). Mass range 9.9e-23 to 7.7e-19 eV as stated in abstract/Eq.47. Assumes ALP constitutes all dark matter with local density rho_0 = 0.3 GeV/cm^3 (Eq. 4). Stochastic bound (kappa=1) chosen as the paper's primary result over the deterministic bound (Eq. 48, dashed). Curve is essentially the linear g ~ m_a relation with mild transfer-function rise at high mass.",
